I'm excited to share the End-to-End Customer Churn Analytics & Prediction Pipeline I built during my internship!🎯

## 📌 Quick Overview:-

1] Goal:- Predict which customers are likely to stop using the service.
2] Output:- A churn probability score (0.0 to 1.0) for every active user.
3] Impact:- Triggers targeted discount emails to bring back at-risk users before they leave.

## 🔄 Project Pipeline:-

* Clean Data:- Remove duplicate records and fix missing values in customer logs.
* Define Churn (SQL):- Analyzed historical orders—90% of repeat users buy within 90 days, so >90 days inactive = Churned.
* Engineer Features:- Calculate inactivity days, recent order counts, and average spend per user.
* Train Model:- Build a binary classifier using time-series split (preventing data leakage).
* Take Action:- Run batch predictions weekly to send promotional emails to high-risk users.

## 🛠️ Key Metrics & Features:-

| Feature Name | Business Hypothesis | SQL Formula |

| days_since_last_order | Inactivity strongly correlates with churn risk. | DATEDIFF(CURRENT_DATE, MAX(order_date)) |
| orders_last_6_months | High recent frequency indicates strong loyalty. | COUNT(order_id) (Last 6 months) |
| avg_order_value | Higher spending tiers exhibit unique retention behaviors. | AVG(total_amount) |

## 🧰 Tech Stack:-

 * Languages:- Python, SQL
 * Libraries:- Pandas, NumPy, Scikit-Learn, XGBoost, Matplotlib
